# Both are optional. Without them, Gmail works via app password (IMAP relay),
# and Outlook users are guided to an .mbox export. Client IDs are public, not secrets.

# Google sign-in ("Connect Gmail"): OAuth 2.0 Client ID, type "Web application".
# Authorized JavaScript origins: http://localhost:5173 (or your dev port) and your deployed URL.
# Enable the Gmail API. Scope used: gmail.modify (read, label, archive, trash, send the
# unsubscribe email; never permanent deletion). It is a restricted scope: while the
# Google Auth Platform app is in "Testing", only listed test users can sign in.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=

# Stay signed in (server-side Google sign-in): the client secret of the same OAuth client.
# Add the redirect URI <origin>/api/google/callback to that client. The refresh token is sealed
# (AES-256-GCM) into an httpOnly cookie; nothing is stored on the server. Without this variable
# the app falls back to the popup sign-in for the current tab, and the map is still cached.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional: a separate random key for sealing session cookies (defaults to a key derived from the secret).
SESSION_SECRET=

# Microsoft sign-in ("Connect Outlook"): Entra ID app registration,
# platform "Single-page application", redirect URI <origin>/redirect.html,
# supported accounts "Any Entra ID tenant + personal Microsoft accounts".
# Delegated permission used: Mail.ReadWrite (read, mark read, move to archive / deleted items / junk).
VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID=
